cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "WideTrail: kernel-checked wide-trail and Poseidon2 bounds in Lean 4"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalisation of the wide trail design strategy. It proves active S-box
  bounds for AES-like designs and Rijndael, concrete AES algebra, exact differential
  trail counts in an independent-key model, partial-round activity bounds for HADES
  and Poseidon2, and certificates for deployed Poseidon2 permutations. Every theorem
  is checked by Lean's kernel, with no axioms beyond propext, Classical.choice and
  Quot.sound.
authors:
